{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Thus said YHWH.</b> Some say that 'His anointed' is the prophet, and some say that it is Cyrus, and both are correct, for the prophet said, 'because He has anointed me' (1 Kings 1), and we also find 'and you shall anoint Hazael' (1 Kings 19:15)." "<b>To descend.</b> The verb is from the conjugation of 'He subdues peoples under me' (Psalms 144:2), and similar is 'for the day when I rise as a witness' (Zephaniah 3:8)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The citation מ\"א א' is ambiguous; resolved as 1 Kings, though the quoted phrase does not correspond to any verse in 1 Kings 1.", 1 "Resolved the root form הרודד as 'He subdues'; the cited Zephaniah phrase appears to differ from the received text וגם עד יום קומי לעד."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:06.790779234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}